  "assumptions": [
    "Each weekday from 4 Jan 2021 through 31 Dec 2025 is one operating day. Four specialty rooms run 08:00\u201316:00.",
    "The list for a room is a fresh weighted draw from the public Specialized inpatient case mix. A case is added while its expected room time still finishes by 16:00.",
    "Expected room time is the sum of the five published interval means. The played duration is one draw from each published distribution, summed and rounded.",
    "A case that has started always finishes, including after 16:00. A case that has not started by 16:00 is cancelled because the room ran out of time.",
    "Three roster labels serve each specialty. One is rostered each weekday. On 6% of rostered days that surgeon is away, and a colleague covers 45% of those days. Otherwise the room's list is cancelled.",
    "Each booked case also has a scenario chance of 1.2% unfit, 0.8% did not attend, 0.5% no bed, and 0.3% equipment. Those chances are assumptions, not measured German rates.",
    "Published day-of-surgery cancellation rates in other hospitals range from under 2% to about 30%. This run is a scenario on public duration distributions, not a forecast for one hospital.",
    "The dollar figure multiplies overtime minutes by $58, rounded from the $57.71 California FY2022 mean operating-room cost reported in JAMA Surgery. It is a published benchmark, shown for scale."
  ],
